# Vercel builds ONLY the Next.js frontend from this monorepo.
#
# Without this, Vercel's framework detection finds apps/api/requirements.txt at
# the repository root, builds the Python API instead of the frontend, and ships
# a deployment with no static output — every route then returns
# FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED. That happened on a git-triggered auto-deploy and
# took the live site down while manual deploys from apps/web kept working,
# which made it invisible until a real browser hit it.
apps/api
services
notebooks
deliverables
scripts
docs
*.zip
